    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitter_lesson",
    "title": "Bitter lesson - Wikipedia",
    "snippet": "The bitter lesson is the observation in artificial intelligence that, in the long run, general approaches that scale with available computational power tend to outperform ones based on domain-specific understanding because they are better at taking advantage of the falling cost of computation over time. The principle was proposed and named in a 2019 essay by Richard Sutton [1] and is now ...   Summarize",
